WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.680
A lone billboard reads nothing—just an empty

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:05.160
space that whispers, "Nothing matters."

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:10.110
Alex feels the weight of a silent

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:12.270
sign, wondering why nothing is written.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.520
The empty space whispers that meaning is

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.580
not waiting, it must be made.

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:24.370
Inside his mind, a dark silhouette asks

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:26.470
what purpose remains when the world offers

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:26.790
none.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.720
Alex realizes that stories he builds become

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:33.460
the light that fills the void.

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:38.490
Sam explains that meaning isn’t discovered but

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:41.070
built, like stacking words into a story

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:42.190
we choose to live.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:47.680
Alex watches the steam rise, realizing each

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.820
breath can become a deliberate chapter.

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:53.130
Alex asks how a fleeting hobby can

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:55.630
feel lasting, and Sam replies that personal

00:00:55.630 --> 00:00:58.790
projects anchor our self‑crafted purpose.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:02.580
Together they sketch a small garden, a

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:04.520
symbol of value grown from their own

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:04.880
hands.

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:10.070
Many think happiness comes from external approval,

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:12.930
like applause or likes, but those sounds

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:15.010
fade when the room goes dark.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:20.040
Alex feels the emptiness deepen, realizing the

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:22.440
party’s glow cannot fill the silence inside.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.250
When the void whispers that nothing matters,

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:29.410
Alex chooses a small project—a sketch of

00:01:29.410 --> 00:01:30.430
a seedling—to nurture.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:34.780
The act of creating a tangible goal

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:37.780
turns the darkness into a quiet, purposeful

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:38.100
light.

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:42.290
The silhouette’s glowing eyes murmur that existence

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:45.890
is empty, and Alex’s breath catches in

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:46.830
the cold hush.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:50.200
The shadow’s voice sharpens, “A sketch?

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:53.470
A tiny, fragile thing?

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:56.080
It will fade, Alex.

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:03.280
The universe is vast and indifferent.

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:06.910
Your little garden will wither.”

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:11.310
Alex’s resolve hardens as he steadies his

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:13.767
hand, willing to confront the silence.

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:18.180
On a sun‑dappled bench, Alex spreads a

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:21.448
sketchpad and begins tracing a blooming seedling.

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:24.670
Each line stitches meaning into the air,

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:27.270
turning idle time into quiet fulfillment.

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:31.320
Alex invites Sam to the bench, unveiling

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:33.460
the sketch that now feels alive.

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:38.010
Together they discuss its colors, realizing a

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:40.310
shared purpose can anchor fleeting thoughts.

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:45.020
Shadow steps forward, voice low and echoing,

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:48.060
"Your meaning is arbitrary, a mere trick

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:48.780
of the mind.

00:02:50.710 --> 00:02:52.730
It holds no weight against the void."

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:58.080
Alex turns, eyes steady, and gestures toward

00:02:58.080 --> 00:02:59.160
the sketchbook on the bench.

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:03.170
"It doesn't need to be absolute to

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:03.710
be real.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:07.560
The fact that I chose this, and

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:09.520
that it anchors my days, makes it

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:10.420
true for me.

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:16.450
The void is empty, but my choice

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:17.070
fills it."

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:21.460
The light isn’t a cure; it’s a

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:23.040
spotlight on his own agency.

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:27.310
The weight of the void doesn’t vanish,

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:29.550
but it becomes a backdrop to his

00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:30.270
active choice.

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:35.740
The freedom of decision feels heavier than

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:38.160
any cosmic promise, yet it steadies his

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:38.480
pulse.

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:43.150
At sunrise, Alex stands on the rooftop,

00:03:43.850 --> 00:03:46.430
the city waking below, his sketchbook warm

00:03:46.430 --> 00:03:47.010
in his hands.

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:51.740
He smiles, accepting that the void still

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:54.300
exists but no longer defines him, and

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.760
that he has built a home within

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:56.400
its silence.

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:03.660
At sunrise, Alex smiles, sketchbook warm, realizing

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:05.600
every line he draws writes his own

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:06.000
purpose.
